WEBVTT

00:02:20.780 --> 00:02:24.000
Futaba-san, do you know who I am-koro?

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:28.340
You're Korori-san, the main character
of the famous anime, <i>Ikinone Korori-chan</i>.

00:02:28.810 --> 00:02:32.180
That's right. And now, I'm your advisor.

00:02:32.180 --> 00:02:32.890
Right.

00:02:32.890 --> 00:02:36.390
Now, Futaba-san, what's going on today-koro?

00:02:36.390 --> 00:02:41.690
Today's the first recording session for the
new spring anime, <i>Buddha Fighter Bodhisattvon</i>!

00:02:42.010 --> 00:02:43.130
That's right.

00:02:43.130 --> 00:02:46.860
<i>Bodhisattvon</i> is an original robot anime
by the world-famous studio Zongo.

00:02:47.410 --> 00:02:51.560
You're playing the mascot character,
so I guess you're part of the main cast,

00:02:51.560 --> 00:02:56.790
but the real big roles belong to the stars and veterans-koro!

00:02:57.490 --> 00:03:02.500
So then, where does that leave
a newbie seiyuu like you-koro?

00:03:03.810 --> 00:03:06.050
It's like... being at an away game.

00:03:06.050 --> 00:03:08.470
But if someone asked,
"When are your home games?"

00:03:08.470 --> 00:03:12.890
I'd say I haven't played one yet.

00:03:12.890 --> 00:03:14.430
That's the wrong attitude-koro!

00:03:19.290 --> 00:03:21.260
But this'll be my first real recording.

00:03:21.260 --> 00:03:23.120
I'm so nervous!

00:03:23.120 --> 00:03:25.860
I wish I could just crawl back into bed...

00:03:26.360 --> 00:03:28.750
But this is your job.

00:03:28.750 --> 00:03:31.830
It's the work of a seiyuu.
You chose this for yourself.

00:03:36.620 --> 00:03:37.830
All right!

00:03:38.750 --> 00:03:40.140
Script, check.

00:03:40.140 --> 00:03:41.290
Cough drops, check.

00:03:41.290 --> 00:03:42.510
Writing implements, check.

00:03:42.510 --> 00:03:43.940
Map to the studio, check.

00:03:43.940 --> 00:03:44.960
Electronic dictionary, check.

00:03:46.010 --> 00:03:47.540
Now, what to wear...

00:03:48.220 --> 00:03:49.090
Out!

00:03:52.270 --> 00:03:53.970
All right, this won't make noise!

00:03:55.360 --> 00:03:57.230
I'm ready!

00:04:00.860 --> 00:04:03.220
I know, Korori-chan.

00:04:08.120 --> 00:04:08.990
Don't worry!

00:04:09.350 --> 00:04:11.990
Someday we'll make it out
of this shabby apartment!

00:04:12.240 --> 00:04:14.990
That's the spirit!
You can do it, Futaba!

00:04:14.990 --> 00:04:18.560
<i>This is the story of newcomer
seiyuu, Ichinose Futaba,</i>

00:04:18.560 --> 00:04:21.520
<i>working passionately
together with her friends,</i>

00:04:21.520 --> 00:04:24.610
<i>running into potholes
and bumps in the road,</i>

00:04:24.610 --> 00:04:27.510
<i>but never giving up on her dream
of becoming a top seiyuu!</i>

00:04:28.230 --> 00:04:29.760
Good morning, Ichinose-san.

00:04:30.200 --> 00:04:32.990
Engaged in pleasant
conversation as usual, I see.

00:04:32.990 --> 00:04:35.420
Oh, g-good morning!

00:04:37.820 --> 00:04:39.660
Hold down the fort, okay?

00:04:39.660 --> 00:04:41.020
Off I go!

00:04:44.900 --> 00:04:47.280
Always arrive early.

00:04:47.650 --> 00:04:49.160
Being late is forbidden!

00:04:49.160 --> 00:04:51.360
The job of bringing
everyone's dreams to life...

00:04:51.360 --> 00:04:53.010
That's what it means to be a seiyuu.

00:04:53.010 --> 00:04:56.300
And this is where
those dreams come... true?!

00:04:58.240 --> 00:04:59.170
Here?

00:04:59.580 --> 00:05:01.460
This <i>is</i> the place, right?

00:05:01.880 --> 00:05:05.490
Studios usually just rent
space in office buildings-koro.

00:05:05.490 --> 00:05:07.750
Of course, there are nice studios, too-koro.

00:05:08.870 --> 00:05:10.590
Good morning...

00:05:14.800 --> 00:05:16.010
Good morning!

00:05:16.010 --> 00:05:16.020
I'm Ichinose Futaba
from Aozora Productions!
Good morning!

00:05:16.020 --> 00:05:18.170
I'm Ichinose Futaba
from Aozora Productions!

00:05:18.170 --> 00:05:19.990
I look forward to working
with you today!

00:05:19.990 --> 00:05:20.890
Morning.

00:05:21.260 --> 00:05:22.520
Good morning!

00:05:22.520 --> 00:05:22.530
I'm Ichinose Futaba
from Aozora Productions!
Good morning!

00:05:22.530 --> 00:05:24.750
I'm Ichinose Futaba
from Aozora Productions!

00:05:24.750 --> 00:05:26.180
I look forward to working
with you today!

00:05:26.180 --> 00:05:27.230
Good morning.

00:05:27.230 --> 00:05:28.510
Good morning!

00:05:28.520 --> 00:05:29.790
I'm Ichinose Futaba
from Aozora Productions!

00:05:29.790 --> 00:05:31.230
First, making the rounds!

00:05:31.230 --> 00:05:35.620
You've gotta greet each person one-by-one.
Just a rule of the business-koro.

00:05:35.950 --> 00:05:38.120
Um, who else...

00:05:38.120 --> 00:05:39.720
Huh?!

00:05:39.720 --> 00:05:41.440
One by one, I said!

00:05:41.440 --> 00:05:44.000
Don't even try to get away
with a mass greeting-koro!

00:05:44.000 --> 00:05:47.750
Who knows, maybe they're lined up
in front of a real famous seiyuu-koro?

00:05:48.080 --> 00:05:50.720
Nice to meet you!

00:05:51.480 --> 00:05:52.880
Good morning!

00:05:52.880 --> 00:05:52.890
I'm Ichinose Futaba
from Aozora Productions!
Good morning!

00:05:52.890 --> 00:05:55.260
I'm Ichinose Futaba
from Aozora Productions!

00:05:55.260 --> 00:05:56.320
Morning.

00:05:56.320 --> 00:05:58.600
Th-That voice is...

00:05:58.600 --> 00:06:00.970
N-N-Nozawa Masako-san?!

00:06:00.970 --> 00:06:03.120
Eh! Nozawa-san, as in <i>that</i> Nozawa-san?

00:06:03.120 --> 00:06:06.520
Does that mean she's gonna shoot energy beams from her hand and transform?!

00:06:06.520 --> 00:06:08.530
N-N-N-Nice to meet you...

00:06:08.530 --> 00:06:10.690
I'm Nozawa. Nice to meet you.

00:06:10.690 --> 00:06:15.740
The pros get to mingle with
super-famous seiyuus all the time-koro.

00:06:15.740 --> 00:06:17.600
My throat hurts...

00:06:17.600 --> 00:06:18.780
Good morning!
Want a cough drop?

00:06:18.780 --> 00:06:20.990
I'm Ichinose Futaba
from Aozora Productions!

00:06:20.990 --> 00:06:22.620
I look forward to working
with you today!

00:06:22.620 --> 00:06:23.500
Same here.

00:06:24.890 --> 00:06:26.110
Good morning!

00:06:26.120 --> 00:06:28.380
I'm Ichinose Futaba
from Aozora Productions!

00:06:28.380 --> 00:06:29.910
I look forward to working
with you today!

00:06:29.910 --> 00:06:31.710
Oh, back at ya.

00:06:31.990 --> 00:06:33.050
Good morning!

00:06:33.610 --> 00:06:35.310
Good morning.

00:06:36.350 --> 00:06:38.320
N-N-Nozawa-san?!

00:06:38.320 --> 00:06:39.110
I'm so sorry!

00:06:39.110 --> 00:06:41.070
I can't believe I greeted you twice!

00:06:41.070 --> 00:06:43.030
It happens all the time.

00:06:44.130 --> 00:06:46.060
You can't even remember people's faces.

00:06:46.060 --> 00:06:48.230
Are you sure you're cut out for this?

00:06:49.950 --> 00:06:52.320
I'm sorry! I'll step it up!

00:06:52.320 --> 00:06:54.640
So where's <i>my</i> greeting?

00:06:54.640 --> 00:06:58.050
I'm so sorry! I'm Ichinose Futaba
from Aozora Productions!

00:06:58.050 --> 00:07:00.300
I look forward to working
with you today!

00:07:00.300 --> 00:07:02.240
One of our newcomers?

00:07:03.150 --> 00:07:05.080
Shiodome Hikari-san!

00:07:05.670 --> 00:07:09.040
Shiodome-san is a senpai from Futaba's agency-koro.

00:07:09.040 --> 00:07:11.790
I-I look forward to working with you.

00:07:11.790 --> 00:07:13.380
Likewise.

00:07:14.970 --> 00:07:17.480
Is there anyone I haven't greeted yet?

00:07:17.480 --> 00:07:18.300
Hm?

00:07:22.970 --> 00:07:25.570
<i>Wow, look at those flashy clothes...</i>

00:07:25.570 --> 00:07:28.230
<i>Oh, but her script has so much writing on it...</i>

00:07:28.520 --> 00:07:29.980
<i>A kindred spirit!</i>

00:07:30.340 --> 00:07:31.650
Good morning!

00:07:31.650 --> 00:07:34.360
I'm Ichinose Futaba
from Aozora Productions!

00:07:34.360 --> 00:07:35.820
Good morning!

00:07:35.820 --> 00:07:39.100
Strawberry
I'm Moesaki Ichigo
from Voice Entertainment!

00:07:39.100 --> 00:07:41.070
Oh? Is that your real name?

00:07:41.330 --> 00:07:45.930
I come from Planet Strawberry
in the Strawberry Nebula!

00:07:45.930 --> 00:07:47.060
Berry!

00:07:49.420 --> 00:07:51.280
Oh, is that right?

00:07:52.100 --> 00:07:53.890
You're just strawberries from head to toe!

00:07:53.890 --> 00:07:58.270
Y-Y-Yes! Well, I just wanted
to make myself memorable...

00:07:58.270 --> 00:08:00.250
Are you really from Planet Strawberry?

00:08:00.250 --> 00:08:01.660
Oh, no! I'm actually
from Kanagawa Prefecture...

00:08:01.660 --> 00:08:03.930
<i>She's already out of character.
Oh, no! I'm actually
from Kanagawa Prefecture...</i>

00:08:03.930 --> 00:08:06.350
Apple
Okay, nice to meet you, Ringo-san.

00:08:06.350 --> 00:08:07.230
It's Ichigo!

00:08:07.230 --> 00:08:08.980
Oh, I'm sorry!

00:08:08.980 --> 00:08:09.020
Oh, I'm sorry!

00:08:12.650 --> 00:08:13.690
Hm?

00:08:13.690 --> 00:08:16.030
There's a little girl in the studio...

00:08:17.060 --> 00:08:18.920
Is everything okay?

00:08:19.530 --> 00:08:21.860
Did you wander in here by accident?

00:08:21.860 --> 00:08:23.870
Uh, no... Um...

00:08:24.200 --> 00:08:26.210
Hey, Rin-chan. Long time no see.

00:08:26.210 --> 00:08:29.270
Oh, Sekigami-san! Good morning!

00:08:29.270 --> 00:08:29.710
Huh?

00:08:29.710 --> 00:08:31.500
You're a third-year now, right?

00:08:31.500 --> 00:08:32.130
Yes!

00:08:32.370 --> 00:08:35.470
Amazing for a middle school student to be working as a seiyuu!

00:08:35.470 --> 00:08:38.620
<i>She's a seiyuu in middle school?!</i>

00:08:39.300 --> 00:08:40.530
See you later, then.

00:08:40.530 --> 00:08:42.640
Nice talking to you!

00:08:43.410 --> 00:08:45.180
I am so terribly sorry!

00:08:45.180 --> 00:08:48.100
I'm Ichinose Futaba
from Aozora Productions.

00:08:48.570 --> 00:08:51.280
I'm Kohana Rin from the
Sakuranbo Theatre Group.

00:08:51.280 --> 00:08:53.350
Nice to meet you!

00:08:53.350 --> 00:08:57.150
You can't judge a seiyuu's career based on their appearance-koro!

00:08:57.150 --> 00:09:01.950
A scrub like you should just assume everyone's
your senpai and greet them accordingly-koro!

00:09:02.190 --> 00:09:04.370
Okay, next is the control room-koro.

00:09:04.790 --> 00:09:09.060
Here's where the recording staff,
anime staff, and various producers

00:09:09.060 --> 00:09:11.370
monitor the seiyuus' performances.

00:09:11.620 --> 00:09:16.880
They've also got audio gear
for mixing, music, and sound effects-koro.

00:09:17.340 --> 00:09:19.340
I look forward to working
with you today!

00:09:19.340 --> 00:09:20.880
Same here.

00:09:21.210 --> 00:09:22.570
Glad to be here.

00:09:22.570 --> 00:09:24.260
This guy's the sound director.

00:09:24.260 --> 00:09:26.520
He's in charge of the whole session-koro.

00:09:26.520 --> 00:09:30.390
Now that we've greeted the staff,
let's head to the recording booth-koro!

00:09:55.630 --> 00:09:58.170
The center seats with the
good view of the monitors

00:09:58.170 --> 00:10:00.990
are where the big names
and people with a lot of lines sit-koro.

00:10:00.990 --> 00:10:04.340
Everyone else chooses their own seats
by just kinda reading the room-koro.

00:10:04.810 --> 00:10:08.960
If you're too slow, you'll end up somewhere
that makes it hard to get to the mic,

00:10:08.960 --> 00:10:11.530
so it's important to secure a seat quickly-koro.

00:10:12.330 --> 00:10:13.310
An open spot!

00:10:13.310 --> 00:10:16.350
But I'm too starstruck
to risk sitting next to her!

00:10:16.350 --> 00:10:18.150
Oh, over there!

00:10:28.750 --> 00:10:30.160
You two over there.

00:10:30.160 --> 00:10:31.240
Hm?

00:10:31.240 --> 00:10:32.580
Those seats are still open.

00:10:33.910 --> 00:10:36.290
Th-Thank you very much!

00:10:40.420 --> 00:10:42.960
Don't you still have things to do-koro?

00:10:43.720 --> 00:10:44.670
<i>All right...</i>

00:10:45.100 --> 00:10:46.090
<i>Turn off my phone,</i>

00:10:46.720 --> 00:10:48.090
<i>look at the script one more time,</i>

00:10:48.460 --> 00:10:50.510
<i>and thank Shiodome-san again.</i>

00:10:51.640 --> 00:10:52.770
Good morning.

00:10:54.850 --> 00:11:00.520
Before they get started, the sound director comes in to make announcements-koro.

00:11:00.870 --> 00:11:03.610
For the first episode,
the series director, scriptwriter,

00:11:03.610 --> 00:11:06.030
and other staff members
may also come say a few words-koro.

00:11:06.300 --> 00:11:11.770
So today, we'll begin recording
<i>Buddha Fighter Bodhisattvon</i>.

00:11:11.770 --> 00:11:15.370
We've got a few revisions to the script.

00:11:15.880 --> 00:11:22.500
Page 4, cut 27. Please change Esta's line,
"Not what I said," to "<i>That's</i> not what I said."

00:11:23.630 --> 00:11:28.910
Page 9, cut 63, Reiji's line,
"You knew, din't you?" is a typo.

00:11:28.910 --> 00:11:31.400
Please make that,
"You knew, didn't you?"

00:11:31.400 --> 00:11:34.460
Page 10, cut 70,
Ellie's line is over the cut.

00:11:34.960 --> 00:11:35.640
"Over the cut?"

00:11:35.870 --> 00:11:40.480
Page 14, cut 115
will break up into A and B.

00:11:41.460 --> 00:11:43.870
<i>"Break up?" Who's breaking up?</i>

00:11:43.870 --> 00:11:47.010
Page 16, cut 147, Gido's line...

00:11:47.010 --> 00:11:50.920
Change "I won't have any regrets!" to "I won't eat anything but durians!"

00:11:50.920 --> 00:11:52.490
What? Why?

00:11:52.490 --> 00:11:54.790
What happened to Gido-san?

00:11:55.050 --> 00:11:59.290
Okay, if there are no questions,
I'd like to start the part A dry run.

00:11:59.700 --> 00:12:01.510
Looking forward to working with you!

00:12:03.570 --> 00:12:05.670
Okay, let's get this show on the road.

00:12:05.990 --> 00:12:08.190
Looking forward
to working with you!

00:12:08.680 --> 00:12:13.180
Before the real thing, there's a dry run
to check everyone's performances-koro.

00:12:20.870 --> 00:12:25.350
The final video often isn't ready in time for the recording phase-koro.

00:12:25.350 --> 00:12:28.190
We apologize to all the seiyuus-koro.

00:12:28.190 --> 00:12:30.400
I think I'll have an omelet today.

00:12:30.400 --> 00:12:32.840
Napolitan pasta sounds
yummy right now.

00:12:32.840 --> 00:12:35.250
There are only three or four mics!

00:12:35.250 --> 00:12:38.200
So you've gotta go up
with perfect timing-koro!

00:12:38.440 --> 00:12:40.460
So this is Planet Zura?

00:12:41.040 --> 00:12:44.750
<i>I can't believe I'm listening
to Nozawa-san's voice in person!</i>

00:12:44.750 --> 00:12:46.550
<i>Oh, right, it's my turn.</i>

00:12:47.050 --> 00:12:49.640
What kind of character
do you play, Futaba-san-koro?

00:12:49.640 --> 00:12:52.130
Pipo is a mascot robot
the main character finds.

00:12:52.660 --> 00:12:56.930
<i>He cries out, "Pipo!" The main character
discovers him, and they become friends.</i>

00:12:57.180 --> 00:13:03.230
<i>His battery's almost drained, but if he's not loud enough, he'll be lost forever.</i>

00:13:03.980 --> 00:13:07.810
<i>What kind of feelings drive
the abandoned Pipo to call out like that?</i>

00:13:07.810 --> 00:13:09.920
<i>Did he use up his last bit of strength?</i>

00:13:09.920 --> 00:13:12.820
<i>Or did he just smile,
resigned to his fate?</i>

00:13:12.820 --> 00:13:16.500
<i>Or was he angry at his former owner
for abandoning him?</i>

00:13:17.160 --> 00:13:18.290
<i>I've got it!</i>

00:13:18.290 --> 00:13:22.540
<i>This Pipo was a super-popular toy
whose owner loved him very much,</i>

00:13:22.760 --> 00:13:26.330
<i>but her parents were always fighting,
and one day she couldn't stand it anymore.</i>

00:13:26.330 --> 00:13:30.410
<i>She and her mother
ended up leaving the house,</i>

00:13:30.410 --> 00:13:32.510
<i>and she brought Pipo with her.</i>

00:13:32.510 --> 00:13:33.520
Way too long-koro!

00:13:33.520 --> 00:13:35.680
And you're changing the story-koro!

00:13:35.680 --> 00:13:38.430
<i>Now, time to show 'em what I've got!</i>

00:13:46.650 --> 00:13:49.230
Pipooooo!

00:13:52.170 --> 00:13:53.050
Huh?

00:13:55.990 --> 00:13:58.720
Okay, good work on the part A dry run.

00:13:58.720 --> 00:14:00.350
<i>Please wait a moment.</i>

00:14:01.450 --> 00:14:05.500
This line right here...
I'd like it to sound cooler.

00:14:05.500 --> 00:14:06.630
I see.

00:14:06.630 --> 00:14:11.420
After the dry run, the staff discuss
how to fine-tune the performances-koro.

00:14:12.240 --> 00:14:13.420
Thanks for waiting.

00:14:14.410 --> 00:14:17.860
Okay, here are the lines that need
to be recorded separately.

00:14:17.860 --> 00:14:18.880
Futaba-san?

00:14:18.880 --> 00:14:21.490
Futaba-san, you don't
have time to be stunned-koro.

00:14:21.490 --> 00:14:23.080
It's almost time for the real thing-koro.

00:14:23.080 --> 00:14:24.560
Futaba-san?!

00:14:24.780 --> 00:14:27.660
Reiji, we're going to record cuts 103 to 107 separately.

00:14:27.660 --> 00:14:28.460
Okay.

00:14:28.460 --> 00:14:30.850
Um, about Esta in this part...

00:14:31.170 --> 00:14:35.920
Should I make her more girly?
A little spoiled and sulky, maybe?

00:14:35.920 --> 00:14:37.680
What you did earlier was fine.

00:14:37.680 --> 00:14:39.310
Don't exaggerate it too much.

00:14:39.310 --> 00:14:40.910
Just act like a normal girl.

00:14:40.910 --> 00:14:42.820
Okay, I understand.

00:14:43.320 --> 00:14:44.700
Pipo-san.

00:14:44.700 --> 00:14:46.660
Ah! Y-Yes?!

00:14:47.030 --> 00:14:50.080
Um, can you do it more normally?

00:14:50.080 --> 00:14:51.650
Normally?

00:14:51.650 --> 00:14:53.040
That's right. Normally.

00:14:53.320 --> 00:14:55.360
O-Okay.

00:14:55.360 --> 00:14:56.560
Normal...

00:14:56.560 --> 00:14:57.930
What is normal?

00:14:57.930 --> 00:15:02.220
Normal for a broken robot who
was thrown away and left for scrap?

00:15:02.700 --> 00:15:05.150
And then for Classmate A—
Normal... Normal... Normal...

00:15:05.150 --> 00:15:05.930
Yes?
Normal... Normal... Normal...

00:15:06.160 --> 00:15:08.600
Can you make it sound
like you have bigger boobs?

00:15:08.600 --> 00:15:10.810
Big boobs?

00:15:10.810 --> 00:15:13.930
Like, you know, use the voice
of someone with bigger boobs.

00:15:13.930 --> 00:15:14.690
Can you do that?

00:15:14.690 --> 00:15:16.970
S-Sure...

00:15:16.970 --> 00:15:18.180
Big boobs...

00:15:22.080 --> 00:15:24.200
Normal... Normal... Normal...

00:15:24.580 --> 00:15:26.200
Okay, let's start the recording.

00:15:26.200 --> 00:15:27.830
C'mon, c'mon, c'mon, c'mon!

00:15:28.260 --> 00:15:30.170
I think I'll have an omelet today.

00:15:30.170 --> 00:15:32.880
Napolitan pasta sounds
yummy right now.

00:15:34.890 --> 00:15:36.230
Pipo!

00:15:36.230 --> 00:15:38.380
<i>Okay, hold it there a sec.</i>

00:15:38.910 --> 00:15:40.880
Can you try that line
a few different ways?

00:15:40.880 --> 00:15:41.970
We'll pick one that works.

00:15:41.970 --> 00:15:43.730
<i>Y-Yes, sir!</i>

00:15:43.730 --> 00:15:47.260
We'd like to explore a few different
merchandising avenues with this series...
<i>Pipo! Pipo! Pipo!</i>

00:15:47.260 --> 00:15:47.790
We'd like to explore a few different
merchandising avenues with this series...

00:15:47.790 --> 00:15:49.760
A web radio show,
events, that kind of thing.

00:15:49.760 --> 00:15:51.390
Sounds like a plan.

00:15:51.390 --> 00:15:53.440
Pipo-san, we've got your line.

00:15:54.220 --> 00:15:56.290
Thank you very much...

00:15:56.900 --> 00:15:59.940
<i>All right, Classmate A,
let's hear your line separately, too.</i>

00:15:59.940 --> 00:16:03.360
Napolitan pasta sounds
yummy right now.

00:16:03.360 --> 00:16:04.770
Okay, one more time.

00:16:04.770 --> 00:16:06.070
<i>Y-Yes, sir!</i>

00:16:06.070 --> 00:16:09.900
But the seiyuus playing the main characters are probably strapped for time.
<i>Napolitan pasta sounds
yummy right now.</i>

00:16:09.900 --> 00:16:14.460
Well, we're trying to keep costs down,
so let's just give the newbies more work.

00:16:14.460 --> 00:16:17.720
We'll just go for something
light and funny.

00:16:18.280 --> 00:16:20.920
<i>Okay, part A's in the books.
Let's take a break.</i>

00:16:22.170 --> 00:16:26.890
After they finish part A, they go through
the same process to record part B-koro.

00:16:29.390 --> 00:16:32.310
Bodhisattvon here, engaging
the hostile Samaya Gaozu soldier!

00:16:32.310 --> 00:16:35.620
Chaturbhuja Embryo,
switch to high morality mode!

00:16:35.620 --> 00:16:38.720
What? Bodhisattvon's
got something like that?

00:16:38.720 --> 00:16:40.420
Awakening fluctuation rate increased.

00:16:40.420 --> 00:16:41.710
Disengage the dry limiter.

00:16:41.710 --> 00:16:44.630
Switch from Mooladhara to
Svadhisthana and Manipura chakras.

00:16:44.630 --> 00:16:49.120
Ten Perfections equalizer, Bodhisattvon,
switch sister program to avatar mode!

00:16:50.120 --> 00:16:51.870
<i>She delivered that doozy of a line...</i>

00:16:51.870 --> 00:16:53.120
<i>...without messing up?!</i>

00:16:57.630 --> 00:17:00.050
<i>So cute!</i>

00:17:00.840 --> 00:17:03.050
<i>This is Bodhisattvon's Kannon history?</i>

00:17:03.590 --> 00:17:05.680
Okay, one moment please.

00:17:05.680 --> 00:17:08.540
Any other parts we need
to record separately for part B?

00:17:08.540 --> 00:17:11.500
The boy's line we added in cut 216.

00:17:11.500 --> 00:17:13.240
Did we forget about that one?

00:17:13.240 --> 00:17:15.690
Oh, you're right. Then...

00:17:16.060 --> 00:17:17.970
<i>Pipo-san, can you do it?</i>

00:17:17.970 --> 00:17:18.730
What?!

00:17:18.730 --> 00:17:20.530
<i>Uh, y-yes sir!</i>

00:17:20.530 --> 00:17:23.650
The boy's line in cut 216.

00:17:23.910 --> 00:17:26.450
Unnamed characters might have one or two lines in a scene.

00:17:26.450 --> 00:17:30.660
Usually, the side characters'
seiyuus handle these parts-koro.

00:17:30.660 --> 00:17:33.330
<i>We'll play it from cut 214.</i>

00:17:37.830 --> 00:17:41.120
That light reathes... Sorry!

00:17:41.120 --> 00:17:42.590
<i>From the top.</i>

00:17:42.820 --> 00:17:46.590
That light reaches innta... Sorry!

00:17:46.590 --> 00:17:48.930
Just relax. Take it nice and easy.

00:17:48.930 --> 00:17:50.840
<i>Okay, sorry!</i>

00:17:51.320 --> 00:17:52.600
One more time.

00:17:53.730 --> 00:17:56.600
That light reaches into the universe.

00:17:57.230 --> 00:17:59.110
<i>Yes! Nailed it!</i>

00:17:59.110 --> 00:18:02.360
<i>You know, that sounded kinda like you were monologuing just now.</i>

00:18:02.360 --> 00:18:05.780
Can you do it less like a monologue
and more like dialogue?

00:18:05.780 --> 00:18:06.860
<i>Y-Yes, sir...</i>

00:18:07.570 --> 00:18:10.030
<i>What's the difference between
a monologue and a line?</i>

00:18:10.030 --> 00:18:12.670
<i>And what's the light
he's talking about, anyway?</i>

00:18:12.670 --> 00:18:15.650
<i>He says it reaches into the universe,
but isn't that just empty space?</i>

00:18:15.650 --> 00:18:18.560
<i>Is it something you can reach,
like you reach someone on the phone?</i>

00:18:18.560 --> 00:18:20.640
<i>Reaching out to someone?
Reaching the end of your rope?</i>

00:18:20.640 --> 00:18:23.130
<i>And is a monologue a line,
or is a line a monologue, or...</i>

00:18:23.530 --> 00:18:25.520
<i>Shiodome-san, can you do it?</i>

00:18:25.520 --> 00:18:26.380
Yes.

00:18:28.680 --> 00:18:30.290
Huh? Huh?

00:18:31.970 --> 00:18:35.560
That light reaches into the universe!

00:18:37.150 --> 00:18:39.360
Okay, that's a wrap. Thanks.

00:18:39.360 --> 00:18:42.310
We're done recording for today.
Good work, everyone.

00:18:42.860 --> 00:18:44.820
Good work!

00:18:49.540 --> 00:18:51.910
Don't worry about it!
That was very sudden.

00:18:52.390 --> 00:18:53.950
N-Nozawa-san?!

00:18:53.950 --> 00:18:56.660
As a seiyuu, you never know
what they'll ask you to do.

00:18:56.950 --> 00:19:02.170
That's why it pays to be
prepared for anything.

00:19:02.570 --> 00:19:04.570
Well, good luck!

00:19:04.570 --> 00:19:05.590
Th-Thank you very mu—

00:19:07.560 --> 00:19:09.470
I-I'm so sorry!

00:19:10.080 --> 00:19:13.470
If you can't handle a short line like that,
you'll never make it as a seiyuu.

00:19:24.230 --> 00:19:26.070
Rain, huh?

00:19:28.430 --> 00:19:30.470
Oh, good work today.

00:19:31.320 --> 00:19:33.360
It's raining, huh?

00:19:33.360 --> 00:19:35.410
I forgot my umbrella.

00:19:36.300 --> 00:19:38.270
You could use mine if you like.

00:19:39.930 --> 00:19:42.590
Kohana... Rin-chan-san?

00:19:42.590 --> 00:19:45.440
Huh? But then you'll get wet...

00:19:45.440 --> 00:19:47.300
I'll be fine!

00:19:47.300 --> 00:19:49.500
You say that, but...

00:19:50.590 --> 00:19:52.350
Good work today!

00:20:04.640 --> 00:20:08.250
She really did a great job
as the operator, didn't she?

00:20:08.250 --> 00:20:10.640
Yeah! Kohana Rin-chan!

00:20:10.640 --> 00:20:13.890
Even though she's only fifteen,
she's got the makings of a pro!

00:20:14.620 --> 00:20:16.380
Disengage the dry limiter!

00:20:16.870 --> 00:20:17.770
That's no good.

00:20:17.770 --> 00:20:19.040
Not operator-like at all.

00:20:19.040 --> 00:20:20.800
What, really?

00:20:20.800 --> 00:20:22.300
Disengage the dry limiter!

00:20:22.300 --> 00:20:24.120
Oh, that sounded like an operator!

00:20:24.120 --> 00:20:24.880
Really?

00:20:24.880 --> 00:20:26.330
Yeah, really!

00:20:26.890 --> 00:20:28.500
Yay!

00:20:28.500 --> 00:20:31.230
All right, I'm not gonna lose to her!

00:20:31.230 --> 00:20:34.830
But I wonder if I'll ever be able to deliver lines like that...

00:20:34.830 --> 00:20:38.010
You totally will! I'm sure of it!

00:20:39.480 --> 00:20:42.820
Hey, why did you want
to become a seiyuu?

00:20:42.820 --> 00:20:43.520
Huh?

00:20:43.770 --> 00:20:46.730
Well... because I like...

00:20:46.730 --> 00:20:47.270
Huh?

00:20:47.540 --> 00:20:49.790
Anime... and games...

00:20:49.790 --> 00:20:50.920
Ah...

00:20:50.920 --> 00:20:52.400
What do you mean, "Ah..."?!

00:20:52.780 --> 00:20:54.730
I'm not some kind of otaku!

00:20:54.730 --> 00:20:57.480
It's not like that's
my gimmick or whatever!

00:20:58.580 --> 00:21:00.410
What about you, Ichinose-san?

00:21:00.410 --> 00:21:05.080
Um, well, when I graduated from school, there wasn't much work available.

00:21:05.080 --> 00:21:08.950
Oh, you tried to become a seiyuu because
it was too hard to find a normal job?

00:21:08.950 --> 00:21:09.770
Yeah.

00:21:10.380 --> 00:21:12.310
What? Is that all a seiyuu is to you?

00:21:12.310 --> 00:21:14.990
You became a seiyuu because
you couldn't land a job?!

00:21:14.990 --> 00:21:17.050
No, that's not how I feel!

00:21:17.050 --> 00:21:18.640
It's more like...

00:21:18.990 --> 00:21:23.910
Since the job market's been so tough,
I would've had a hard time in any field...

00:21:24.400 --> 00:21:26.010
So I figured,

00:21:26.880 --> 00:21:29.650
if I was going to be
in for a fight anyway,

00:21:29.930 --> 00:21:34.570
I might as well fight to make
my biggest dream come true.

00:21:36.180 --> 00:21:37.660
And that's to be a seiyuu!

00:21:38.020 --> 00:21:39.660
To do work with my voice!

00:21:51.170 --> 00:21:52.850
Well, I'm going this way.

00:21:52.850 --> 00:21:54.170
See you next week, then.

00:21:54.500 --> 00:21:55.970
Let's do our best, Futaba!

00:21:55.970 --> 00:21:58.740
Yeah, let's work hard, Ringo-san!

00:21:59.400 --> 00:22:00.620
You got my name wrong again!

00:22:00.620 --> 00:22:02.640
I-I'm sorry, Ichigo-san!

00:22:02.640 --> 00:22:04.700
Well, see you next week!

00:22:04.700 --> 00:22:09.050
Jeez! Make sure you
get it right next time!

00:22:09.050 --> 00:22:10.570
Okay!
